 how much confident you are about an investement. If you have 20 years of experience, now everything about the company and you are sure there will be profit you can concentrate. If you are not 100% sure there will be a profit, it is better to Diversify. Diversifying can also be profitating when you loose money: because you will pay tax when you earn money, if you diversify you can choose to loose money in some stock (usually in december) and in this way cut your taxes.",
    "statements": [
        "The reference recommends diversification for beginner investors.",
        "Beginner investors should avoid investing all available investment money in a single company.",
        "Diversification reduces the risk of losing the entire investment if a single company fails, according to page 1 of the reference.",
        "The reference suggests considering a simple index-fund portfolio.",
        "A contributor invests 10% of every paycheck across Canadian, U.S., and international TD e-series index funds.",
        "The contributor's investment approach is an example rather than a prescribed allocation for all investors, according to page 1 of the reference.",
        "The reference recommends paying attention to investment costs and portfolio maintenance.",
        "The contributor highlights low management fees.",
        "The contributor highlights the ability to rebalance monthly without commission fees.",
        "An easy-to-manage portfolio can be suitable for investors beyond beginners, according to page 1 of the reference.",
        "The reference recommends understanding retirement-account taxes.",
        "The reference describes deductible IRA contributions on page 1.",
        "The reference describes tax-free growth inside an IRA on page 1.",
        "The reference describes ordinary-income taxation on IRA withdrawals on page 1.",
        "The reference describes an additional 10% penalty for IRA withdrawals before retirement age on page 1.",
        "The reference does not provide a personalized asset allocation.",
        "The reference does not provide specific fund weights."
    ]
}
